  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Conference for Prosecutors on the accountability for conflict-related sexual violence in Sub-Sahara Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UN Team of Experts on the Rule of Law and Sexual Violence in Conflict, together with the Netherlands and Kenya (TBC), will host the first Regional Conference of Prosecutors on Accountability for Conflict-Related Sexual Violence on 14&#x2013;15 October 2026 in Nairobi. It brings together prosecutors and legal practitioners from Sub-Saharan Africa, alongside colleagues from international tribunals, civil society, and prosecutors from other regions will be invited. The conference builds on the international conference the Netherlands hosted in The Hague in March 2024, and on the global CRSV Prosecution Network launched at CSW70 in March 2026.

The objective is to strengthen accountability for CRSV by advancing effective prosecutorial practice in the region: sharing successful approaches, identifying common challenges and solutions, fostering judicial cooperation on cross-border crimes, and reinforcing peer support among prosecutors handling CRSV cases.</narrative>
  </description>
